# Root Dockerfile's build context is the repo root (`COPY . .`). .gitignore
# keeps these out of the repo, but that offers no protection at build time —
# a local .env or uncommitted key sitting in the working tree gets copied
# into the image layer history regardless of git status unless it's excluded
# here too.
#
# Every pattern below is anchored with `**/` where it should match at any
# depth. A bare `*.key` matches ONLY the context root: Docker's exclusion
# patterns are matched against the path relative to the context, so `*.key`
# never matched `scripts/local/deploy.key` and `.env` never matched
# `web/console/.env`. That is the opposite of what a secret exclusion is for,
# and the bare forms read as if they already covered it.

.git/
.github/

# Secrets & key material — never bake into an image layer.
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/*.cer
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx

# The disposable local stand (scripts/pentest-stand.sh). It holds a generated
# admin secret, JWT secret, propagation secret and the report SIGNING key —
# the key that attests audit evidence. It is gitignored, so nothing kept it
# out of a build context until now.
.stand/

# Issued license files / hardware-grace state (internal/license,
# cmd/licensegen) — not key material, but customer-identifying (licensee,
# hardware fingerprint); no reason to sit in a build-cache layer's history.
**/*.lic
**/*.hwgrace

# Build artifacts / local state not needed to compile the gateway binary.
**/*.test
**/*.out
**/coverage.*
**/*.coverprofile
**/profile.cov
/bin/
/load
**/*.rdb
gosec_results.json

# Frontend toolchain output — the gateway build only needs the already-
# committed internal/api/console_dist, never node_modules or a dev cache.
**/node_modules/
**/.vite/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
web/v3/dist/
web/pilot-requests.jsonl

# Local working notes and third-party linter scratch state.
handoff.md
.aislop/

# Editor / OS junk.
.vscode/
.idea/
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*~
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.log
**/*.tmp
**/*.bak
**/*.orig
**/*.rej

# Presentation/scratch material that has no business in a build context.
docs/assets/
